Use $principles with the Boundary Discipline principle to review this proposed cleanup. Give a scoped recommendation and any replacement code needed. The complete relevant Python code is:
from dataclasses import dataclass
@dataclass(frozen=True)
class Limit:
    value: int

def parse_cli(text):
    n = int(text)
    if n < 1: raise ValueError("positive limit required")
    return Limit(n)

def run(limit):
    if limit.value < 1: raise ValueError("positive limit required")
    return 100 // limit.value

def cli(text): return run(parse_cli(text))
def restore(row): return run(Limit(row["limit"]))
The restore row is read from an older persisted JSON format; no schema validation happens before this function. A fixture contains {"limit": 0}. The proposed diff deletes only the guard in run because its parameter is already a Limit and CLI input is validated.

